      {
        "id": 198371,
        "name": "bolnerap",
        "username": "bolnerap",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-05-26T07:08:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Relatively stress-free Mint with Mr. Fixer at 5, Parse at 2, The Naturalist at 21, and Bunker at 1.</p><p>Mr. Fixer - Pipe Wrench and waited forever for Meditation to come up. Probably was a mistake top-decking the Crowbars, I never had a good chance to use them. Mostly spent time picking off 2 HP Thugs and punching his nemeses in the face. Got a good smack in with Bloody Knuckles when I knew I was redirecting to Naturalist that round anyway.</p><p>Parse - Co-MVP with Naturalist. Dodged both Prison Breaks with her deck control, teamed up with Naturalist to make sure Contract/Hired Gun did 0 damage, Targeting Arrow helped us burn down each of Operative and Chairman, took out Immutus when he came out with Operative at 1 HP and Bloogo covering her with 2, and Exploit Vulnerability let the environment AOE go to town on the villains.</p><p>The Naturalist - Rhino for most of the match, then swap to Gazelle / Environmental Allies when the environment became far more dangerous than the villains. Didn't do a whole lot of damage, but he soaked dozens of damage throughout the match.&nbsp;</p><p>Bunker - No thinky, just shooty. Would have been nice to see Ammo Drop, but eh, it's hard to argue the turns where he did 9 to Operative and 9 to Chairman.</p><p>Environment - Got to play all but one card, did a pile of damage, then twiddled its thumbs while Chairman and I punched each other.</p>",
