        "created_at": "2017-05-30T14:59:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"scifantasy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/scifantasy/48/2070_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> scifantasy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>UXM266 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Lord Flash Fire wrote:<br><blockquote>&nbsp;UXM266 wrote:<br><blockquote>I failed numerous times. I don't know how to use Parse properly in this game. I really do suck at playing that long game.&nbsp;&nbsp;Not it for me .&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nIt's okay. The only person I know how to play Parse well against is Apostate.\n</blockquote>\nIt's a cool setup, I do dig it! It's not impossible, or boring. it's just hard. I just don't know which deck to stack, and how.&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThe Chairman's, every chance you get. Neutralize Prison Break, get the Underbosses into the trash, anything you can do to stop the bum rush.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><br>I stacked the Environment deck until Slamara was on top, and then focused on the Chairman.</p>",
